      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To counteract \"bad faith\" actors, incorporate stringent change order protocols requiring written, approved documentation for any deviations, including fee changes. You should enforce comprehensive audit rights allowing your firm to regularly inspect their operations, quality controls, and invoicing records. Additionally, define clear penalties for material misrepresentation or intentional delays to establish strong deterrents against supplier malfeasance.",
      "source": "target",
