      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The best defense against subtle undermining is strong, measurable performance metrics beyond simple delivery dates. Incorporate a \"Good Faith Obligation\" clause, legally requiring the supplier to act with honesty and transparency in all dealings, which gives you grounds for dispute resolution. Furthermore, require detailed communication logs and standardized reporting on potential risks, making hidden issues visible and auditable.",
      "source": "target",
